{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012HaGEdntzoTrLJa8dTZE1s","type":"tool_result","content":"1\texperiments:\n2\t  # === P0: Must-run experiments (headline results) ===\n3\t\n4\t  - id: plan_001\n5\t    claim: 2\n6\t    name: feature_ablation_and_trend\n7\t    description: >\n8\t      Three-part analysis on existing MVP data (zero new generation):\n9\t      (A) Feature ablation: reference-model-only features (entropy_mean/std/min/max + tail_decay)\n10\t      vs surface-only features (TTR + hapax_ratio) vs full feature set. XGBoost 5-fold CV for each.\n11\t      (B) H1/H2 trend analysis: plot each feature's mean ± std across depth 0-4. Monotonic trend → H2 (divergence);\n12\t      plateau → H1 (convergence). Fit linear regression per feature, report slope + R².\n13\t      (C) Perplexity pre-validation for Claim 3: compute Pythia-410M perplexity on depth-stratified subsets\n14\t      (no fine-tuning, just forward pass). If perplexity varies significantly with depth → Claim 3 signal exists.\n15\t    priority: P0\n16\t    gpu_budget_hours: 1\n17\t    deps: [mvp-001]\n18\t    notes: >\n19\t      Uses existing MVP data + features.csv. Critical for Claim 2.\n20\t      Plan B if surface-only ≈ full: reframe Claim 2 as \"complementary signal\" instead of \"independent signal\",\n21\t      narrative shifts to \"vocabulary impoverishment as primary depth signal\".\n22\t\n23\t  - id: plan_002\n24\t    claim: 1\n25\t    name: cross_generator_evaluation\n26\t    description: >\n27\t      Expand to 5 generators (Pythia-2.8B, OLMo-2-1B, Qwen3.5-2B, Qwen3.5-0.8B, Pythia-1B).\n28\t      Leave-one-generator-out CV to test cross-generator generalization.\n29\t      1000 seeds × 5 generators × 5 depths = 25K chains.\n30\t    priority: P0\n31\t    gpu_budget_hours: 20\n32\t    deps: [plan_001]\n33\t    notes: >\n34\t      Only proceed if plan_001 confirms reference features have independent or complementary value.\n35\t      Pythia family overlap (2.8B + 1B): supplement with leave-one-family-out evaluation in analysis.\n36\t      Discuss limitation in paper if Pythia holdout performance inflated by Pythia-1B in training set.\n37\t\n38\t  - id: plan_003\n39\t    claim: 1\n40\t    name: cross_family_reference_model\n41\t    description: >\n42\t      Test non-Pythia reference models (OLMo-2-1B, Qwen3.5-0.8B) for feature extraction.\n43\t      Addresses RC2 — verifies signal isn't architecture-specific artifact.\n44\t    priority: P0\n45\t    gpu_budget_hours: 8\n46\t    deps: [plan_002]\n47\t\n48\t  - id: plan_004\n49\t    claim: 3\n50\t    name: downstream_utility\n51\t    description: >\n52\t      RQ4: Fine-tune a small LM (Pythia-410M or OLMo-1B) on depth-stratified data subsets.\n53\t      Measure perplexity degradation on held-out test set as function of training data depth.\n54\t      Compare depth-aware filtering vs binary baselines (FastDetectGPT, LD-Score threshold).\n55\t    priority: P0\n56\t    gpu_budget_hours: 15\n57\t    deps: [plan_002]\n58\t\n59\t  # === P1: Important for story completeness ===\n60\t\n61\t  - id: plan_005\n62\t    claim: 1\n63\t    name: prompt_type_comparison\n64\t    description: >\n65\t      RQ2 partial: Compare continuation vs elaboration vs inspired_rewriting chains.\n66\t      Tests whether semantic divergence from source correlates with depth signal preservation.\n67\t      Same 1000 seeds, Pythia-2.8B, 3 prompt types.\n68\t    priority: P1\n69\t    gpu_budget_hours: 10\n70\t    deps: [plan_001]\n71\t\n72\t  - id: plan_006\n73\t    claim: 1\n74\t    name: paraphrastic_comparison\n75\t    description: >\n76\t      RQ2 full: Construct parallel paraphrasing chains for direct comparison with continuation chains.\n77\t      Tests attractor convergence theory — do non-paraphrastic chains preserve more depth signal?\n78\t    priority: P1\n79\t    gpu_budget_hours: 8\n80\t    deps: [plan_005]\n81\t\n82\t  - id: plan_007\n83\t    claim: 1\n84\t    name: cross_model_chains\n85\t    description: >\n86\t      RQ3: Cross-model chains (different generator per depth step) vs single-model chains.\n87\t      More realistic scenario — web contamination involves diverse generators.\n88\t    priority: P1\n89\t    gpu_budget_hours: 12\n90\t    deps: [plan_002]\n91\t\n92\t  - id: plan_008\n93\t    claim: 1\n94\t    name: multi_domain_seeds\n95\t    description: >\n96\t      Expand seeds to 4 domains: Wikipedia, news (CNN/DailyMail), scientific (S2ORC abstracts),\n97\t      creative writing (WritingPrompts). 500 seeds per domain × 5 depths.\n98\t    priority: P1\n99\t    gpu_budget_hours: 10\n100\t    deps: [plan_002]\n101\t\n102\t  # === P2: Nice-to-have / strengthen claims ===\n103\t\n104\t  - id: plan_009\n105\t    claim: 1\n106\t    name: finer_grained_ordinal\n107\t    description: >\n108\t      Secondary analysis: 5-class ordinal classification (gen-0 through gen-4)\n109\t      on non-paraphrastic chains. Tests if more depth signal exists beyond 3-class.\n110\t    priority: P2\n111\t    gpu_budget_hours: 1\n112\t    deps: [plan_002]\n113\t\n114\t  - id: plan_010\n115\t    claim: 1\n116\t    name: human_edit_robustness\n117\t    description: >\n118\t      RC5: Robustness to simulated human edits.\n119\t      (A) Random word replacement (5%, 10%, 20%) as lower-bound.\n120\t      (B) LLM-simulated editing (light rephrasing of random sentences).\n121\t    priority: P2\n122\t    gpu_budget_hours: 5\n123\t    deps: [plan_002]\n124\t\n125\t  - id: plan_011\n126\t    claim: 2\n127\t    name: ld_score_feature\n128\t    description: >\n129\t      Add LD-Score (character-distribution signature from arXiv:2605.01647) as additional feature.\n130\t      Tests whether character-level features provide complementary depth signal.\n131\t    priority: P2\n132\t    gpu_budget_hours: 2\n133\t    deps: [plan_001]\n134\t\n135\t  - id: plan_012\n136\t    claim: 1\n137\t    name: end_to_end_classifier\n138\t    description: >\n139\t      QLoRA fine-tuned Qwen3.5-0.8B for end-to-end depth classification.\n140\t      Compares learned representations vs handcrafted distributional features.\n141\t    priority: P2\n142\t    gpu_budget_hours: 15\n143\t    deps: [plan_002]\n144\t\n145\t# GPU Budget Summary:\n146\t# P0: ~44 GPU·hours\n147\t# P1: ~40 GPU·hours\n148\t# P2: ~23 GPU·hours\n149\t# Total: ~107 GPU·hours (well within 200 H100-hour budget; RTX 5090 ≈ H100 throughput for small models)\n150\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7226ef14-9202-402e-bf16-59eaf3672a72","uuid":"a5dad07b-a7a8-43be-81ed-d3c54a589648","timestamp":"2026-05-14T18:19:30.450Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_3/projects/gen-depth-fingerprint/experiment_plan.yaml","content":"experiments:\n  # === P0: Must-run experiments (headline results) ===\n\n  - id: plan_001\n    claim: 2\n    name: feature_ablation_and_trend\n    description: >\n      Three-part analysis on existing MVP data (zero new generation):\n      (A) Feature ablation: reference-model-only features (entropy_mean/std/min/max + tail_decay)\n      vs surface-only features (TTR + hapax_ratio) vs full feature set. XGBoost 5-fold CV for each.\n      (B) H1/H2 trend analysis: plot each feature's mean ± std across depth 0-4. Monotonic trend → H2 (divergence);\n      plateau → H1 (convergence). Fit linear regression per feature, report slope + R².\n      (C) Perplexity pre-validation for Claim 3: compute Pythia-410M perplexity on depth-stratified subsets\n      (no fine-tuning, just forward pass). If perplexity varies significantly with depth → Claim 3 signal exists.\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 1\n    deps: [mvp-001]\n    notes: >\n      Uses existing MVP data + features.csv. Critical for Claim 2.\n      Plan B if surface-only ≈ full: reframe Claim 2 as \"complementary signal\" instead of \"independent signal\",\n      narrative shifts to \"vocabulary impoverishment as primary depth signal\".\n\n  - id: plan_002\n    claim: 1\n    name: cross_generator_evaluation\n    description: >\n      Expand to 5 generators (Pythia-2.8B, OLMo-2-1B, Qwen3.5-2B, Qwen3.5-0.8B, Pythia-1B).\n      Leave-one-generator-out CV to test cross-generator generalization.\n      1000 seeds × 5 generators × 5 depths = 25K chains.\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 20\n    deps: [plan_001]\n    notes: >\n      Only proceed if plan_001 confirms reference features have independent or complementary value.\n      Pythia family overlap (2.8B + 1B): supplement with leave-one-family-out evaluation in analysis.\n      Discuss limitation in paper if Pythia holdout performance inflated by Pythia-1B in training set.\n\n  - id: plan_003\n    claim: 1\n    name: cross_family_reference_model\n    description: >\n      Test non-Pythia reference models (OLMo-2-1B, Qwen3.5-0.8B) for feature extraction.\n      Addresses RC2 — verifies signal isn't architecture-specific artifact.\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 8\n    deps: [plan_002]\n\n  - id: plan_004\n    claim: 3\n    name: downstream_utility\n    description: >\n      RQ4: Fine-tune a small LM (Pythia-410M or OLMo-1B) on depth-stratified data subsets.\n      Measure perplexity degradation on held-out test set as function of training data depth.\n      Compare depth-aware filtering vs binary baselines (FastDetectGPT, LD-Score threshold).\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 15\n    deps: [plan_002]\n\n  # === P1: Important for story completeness ===\n\n  - id: plan_005\n    claim: 1\n    name: prompt_type_comparison\n    description: >\n      RQ2 partial: Compare continuation vs elaboration vs inspired_rewriting chains.\n      Tests whether semantic divergence from source correlates with depth signal preservation.\n      Same 1000 seeds, Pythia-2.8B, 3 prompt types.\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 10\n    deps: [plan_001]\n\n  - id: plan_006\n    claim: 1\n    name: paraphrastic_comparison\n    description: >\n      RQ2 full: Construct parallel paraphrasing chains for direct comparison with continuation chains.\n      Tests attractor convergence theory — do non-paraphrastic chains preserve more depth signal?\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 8\n    deps: [plan_005]\n\n  - id: plan_007\n    claim: 1\n    name: cross_model_chains\n    description: >\n      RQ3: Cross-model chains (different generator per depth step) vs single-model chains.\n      More realistic scenario — web contamination involves diverse generators.\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 12\n    deps: [plan_002]\n\n  - id: plan_008\n    claim: 1\n    name: multi_domain_seeds\n    description: >\n      Expand seeds to 4 domains: Wikipedia, news (CNN/DailyMail), scientific (S2ORC abstracts),\n      creative writing (WritingPrompts). 500 seeds per domain × 5 depths.\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 10\n    deps: [plan_002]\n\n  # === P2: Nice-to-have / strengthen claims ===\n\n  - id: plan_009\n    claim: 1\n    name: finer_grained_ordinal\n    description: >\n      Secondary analysis: 5-class ordinal classification (gen-0 through gen-4)\n      on non-paraphrastic chains. Tests if more depth signal exists beyond 3-class.\n    priority: P2\n    gpu_budget_hours: 1\n    deps: [plan_002]\n\n  - id: plan_010\n    claim: 1\n    name: human_edit_robustness\n    description: >\n      RC5: Robustness to simulated human edits.\n      (A) Random word replacement (5%, 10%, 20%) as lower-bound.\n      (B) LLM-simulated editing (light rephrasing of random sentences).\n    priority: P2\n    gpu_budget_hours: 5\n    deps: [plan_002]\n\n  - id: plan_011\n    claim: 2\n    name: ld_score_feature\n    description: >\n      Add LD-Score (character-distribution signature from arXiv:2605.01647) as additional feature.\n      Tests whether character-level features provide complementary depth signal.\n    priority: P2\n    gpu_budget_hours: 2\n    deps: [plan_001]\n\n  - id: plan_012\n    claim: 1\n    name: end_to_end_classifier\n    description: >\n     